## Goal
Make `SetUnwrap` in `internal/rulesfile/unwrap.go` save the Settings unwrap options without losing or multiplying comments in the user's rules file (DEV-48). Saving must be idempotent.

## Problems
- QA of the earlier fix (7687fe0) found a new defect. A trailing comment on `unwrap_skip_openers:` was copied into the loose comments and also re-attached to the key line. Every save added another copy, so the file grew.
- Loose comments were collected by ranging over a Go map. Their order changed between runs when both keys carried comments and the options were reset to defaults.
- The trailing-comment parser gave up whenever the text before `#` contained a quote. A comment after `["com.a"]` was lost.

## Decision
- Only comments of keys that are no longer written are moved to their own lines. Comments of keys that are written stay on the key line and are not copied a second time.
- The loose comments are emitted in a fixed key order (`unwrap`, then `unwrap_skip_openers`), so the output is deterministic.
- `trailingComment` now tracks quote state and recognises `#` only outside quotes. Comments after quoted values are kept, and a `#` inside a quoted string is not mistaken for a comment.
- Keys stay at their original positions, so repeated saves give the same text.
- Added tests in `internal/rulesfile/unwrap_test.go` for save-twice idempotence, comment order and quoted trailing comments.

## Rejected
None. QA's suggestion to delete each comment from `trailing` once used was an equivalent option, and the fixed-order emission of unused-key comments was chosen instead.

## Touched
`internal/rulesfile` (`unwrap.go`, `unwrap_test.go`), Settings endpoint `/api/settings/unwrap` (caller), `make test`.
